{"name":"Intuitive","hex":"#cfc6bc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"intuitive","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Spontaneous, without requiring conscious thought.","Easily understood or grasped by intuition."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who has (especially parapsychological) intuition."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intuitive"}],"entries":[{"title":"Intuition","blocks":[{"text":"Intuition is the ability to acquire knowledge without recourse to conscious reasoning or needing an explanation. Different fields use the word \"intuition\" in very different ways, including but not limited to: direct access to unconscious knowledge; unconscious cognition; gut feelings; inner sensing; inner insight to unconscious pattern-recognition; and the ability to understand something instinctively, without any need for conscious reasoning. Intuitive knowledge tends to be approximate or heuristic."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intuition","wikidata":"Q189222"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"intuitive":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/40/En-GB-intuitive.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/40/En-GB-intuitive.ogg/En-GB-intuitive.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a2/En-us-intuitive.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/a2/En-us-intuitive.ogg/En-us-intuitive.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share